# exp-followup-4-bind-resolution audit — notes

Audit of commit e25e0aedec42f3e1ea475e642384e3b2ab1499b3, build Run
20261116T031033Z-submit-muse-code-muse-wonder-1.0-c1.

## Lessons

- Fixtures pass (`./test/harness.sh` → `harness.sh: all checks passed`),
  but live resolution still refuses: `bp3 harness find-tape --run-id
  20261116T031033Z-submit-muse-code-muse-wonder-1.0-c1` returned
  E_AMBIGUOUS naming 4 real tapes. The fixture author's entry binds
  `BP3_RUN_ID=<run>` to the submit call in one line; the live author's
  entry does not (env-stamped run-id, no literal prefix), so the
  own-edge filter finds no unique tape on the real sibling set.
- No bind happened for the build Run: its derivation log
  (`<git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/20261116T031033Z-submit-muse-code-muse-wonder-1.0-c1.jsonl`)
  holds only the init_record row, and the supervisor folds that Run as
  lifecycle `init`, not `finished`. Hence `live bind` fails.
- Zero whole-tape (rung 5b) reads; no rung 5a pointer exists to resolve
  (derivation log has no pointer rows, find-tape refuses before entry
  resolution). All rows decided at rungs 1–3.
- Pre-existing dirty tapes in other exps' run folders are not part of
  commit e25e; the commit itself is clean (4 files).

