# followup.4 bind-resolution — check notes (cycle 1, commit e25e0ae)

Verdict: fail. Fixtures green, live bind still refuses.

- `make check` green and `./test/harness.sh` prints "all checks passed":
  the followup.4 sibling fixtures (init/resolve/conductor/author) resolve
  as designed, and `narrow_candidates` (src/quest/harness.ml:1100) is
  shared by `do_find_tape` (:1190) and `resolve_watch` (:1366).
- Fresh live probe at e25e0ae:
  `./bin/bp3 harness find-tape --run-id 20261116T031033Z-submit-muse-code-muse-wonder-1.0-c1`
  still returns `E_AMBIGUOUS` naming four candidate tapes. The gated
  "live bind" acceptance case therefore fails; a fresh submit Run would
  still not bind post-author.
- Diagnosis (whole-tape grep, escalation: confused — fixtures pass but
  live refuses): the author's tape has 7 lines binding
  `BP3_RUN_ID=<submit-run>` to `u exp-followup-4-bind-resolution submit`,
  but the conductor `session.jsonl` has 3 such lines too — it quotes the
  child's brief, which contains the full prefixed edge invocation. The
  own-edge filter finds two tapes, not one, and refuses by design.
- Lesson: quoting is not just run-id mention. Any tape that quotes the
  workflow brief verbatim carries the own-edge invocation textually, so
  per-line co-occurrence cannot separate author from quoting conductor.
  A stronger signal is needed (e.g. tool-call entries vs prompt text, or
  excluding entries whose payload kind is the brief itself).
- Adherence held: clean 4-file commit, submit ledger line stamps the
  env-set run-id, build run folder carries tape.log and notes.md, and
  state moved only via the bp3 state commit.

