1905:  bp3 harness bind-tape --run-id <id> --tape-path <p>   launcher binds a finished child's session tape after it returns (pointer-only tape_binding row)\n\
1914:  Mechanism (mvp.4): each changed tick appends one pointer-only observation row to the Run's own <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl (keyed by run-id; session-id is only an InitRecord field) and refreshes its disposable <run-id>.json cache. Since mvp.5 the derivation logs are the sole lifecycle read path; the retired shared maps are never read or written. Writer discipline (followup.1): each row is a single write() on an O_APPEND descriptor and the cache is a uniquely named temp file in the same directory, fsynced and renamed over the old cache, so parallel supervisors never tear a row or the cache; a torn final line is ignored by the fold and reported as W_TORN_TAIL. Tape binding (followup.3): when the InitRecord names no tape, the latest pointer-only tape_binding row in the same log names it; with no tape at all the probe is blind (W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND) and the lifecycle stays init.\n\
1950:  Appends one pointer-only tape_binding row (run-id, tape path, timestamp; never tape content) as a single write to <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl, after the child returns and its session tape has closed. The fold names the tape from the InitRecord's own tape path, else the latest binding; a missing tape path is never guessed. A run-id with no InitRecord is E_NOT_FOUND; a bad run-id or a missing, duplicate, or =-formed flag is E_USAGE. Emits {ok, run_id, tape_path, path}.\n\
1955:  Appends the first derivation row (kind init_record) to <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl before the child starts, so find-tape/watch/supervisor resolve the Run from birth. Create-only: an existing log for the run-id is E_EXISTS; a bad run-id, engine, or pid is E_USAGE. Emits {ok, run_id, harness, session_id, pid, tape_path, quest, exp, path}.\n\
